ENGLISH
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. Subject
   ortino.CAM (the "Program") consists of the application, its source code, the bundled examples, fonts and data files, and
   the documentation. The Program is protected by copyright and is not open-source software. Third-party components are
   licensed under their own licenses (section 6).

2. Right of use
   The copyright holder grants you a simple, non-exclusive, non-transferable, non-sublicensable right to install the Program,
   in the version provided by the copyright holder (installer, updates), on your own computers and to use it to plan and
   manufacture your own workpieces – privately and commercially.

3. Not permitted without the written consent of the copyright holder
   a) passing on, selling, renting, lending or publicly making available the Program or parts of it;
   b) modifying, reverse-engineering, decompiling or disassembling the Program, except where mandatory law allows it;
   c) removing or changing copyright, license or origin notices;
   d) operating the Program or the community portal as a service for third parties, or operating further portals in the
      name of ortino.CAM (there is exactly one official portal, hosted by the operator);
   e) using the name "ortino.CAM" or its mark for your own products without consent.

4. Your content
   Your projects, drawings and generated files (e.g. .ocam, DXF, SVG, G-code) belong to you; the Program claims no rights in
   them. Designs from the community portal are subject to the terms their authors stated when sharing them and to the
   portal's terms of use.

5. Safety, disclaimer of warranty and liability
   a) CNC machines can injure people and damage property. The Program creates toolpaths and G-code to the best of its
      knowledge; before every job you must check the simulation, the checklist and the program yourself (first without tool
      and material), keep the emergency stop within reach and never leave the machine unattended. Simulation, checklist and
      pre-flight check are aids, not safety functions.
   b) The Program is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, in particular none for freedom from defects, fitness
      for a particular purpose, availability or particular properties. You use it at your own risk. The Program was
      developed mostly with AI assistance and has been tested on real machines only in part.
   c) The copyright holder and everyone who contributed to the Program are not liable for damages arising from the use of,
      or the inability to use, the Program – in particular injury, damage to machine, tool and workpiece, fire,
      consequential damages, lost profit and loss of data – to the extent permitted by law.
   d) Liability for intent, for injury to life, body or health, under the product liability act, and where mandatory law
      requires it, remains unaffected.

6. Third-party components
   ortino.CAM contains third-party software and fonts (Rust libraries, JavaScript libraries, the DejaVu and Inter fonts).
   They are governed by their own licenses; names, authors and license texts are listed in THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt
   (installation folder; in the program under "About ortino.CAM → Licenses"). Where one of those licenses grants broader
   rights, these rights remain unaffected.

7. Termination, governing law
   The right of use ends if you violate these terms. The law of the Federal Republic of Germany applies, excluding the UN
   Convention on Contracts for the International Sale of Goods, unless mandatory consumer protection law provides otherwise.
